    "result_text": "All 281 tests pass, including the new `Cp18Tests`. \n\nThe change is complete. To implement the `locality` field on owner creation, I:\n\n1. **`AssignLocality.java`** (new function) \u2014 computes, at creation time before save, the most common city among existing owners. Sets `locality` to `\"local\"` only when there is a *single* most common city (no tie) that matches the new owner's city; otherwise `\"remote\"`. Cities are grouped case-insensitively, matching the existing city-handling functions, and it runs after `normalizeCity` so it compares canonical spellings.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `assignLocality` step into the pipeline (after `assignSharesHousehold`, before `save`, under the same `transaction` governance).\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `locality` field with `@Column(name = \"locality\")` and getter/setter, so it persists and is returned on later `GET` (the test fetches the owner fresh).\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it by name automatically).\n\n5. **Schema/data files** \u2014 added the `locality` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) and a trailing `NULL` to the positional owner inserts in `hsqldb/data.sql` (the h2 and postgres data scripts use explicit column lists, so they needed no change).",
